1
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:34,890
[OVERDO]

2
00:01:35,430 --> 00:01:37,830
[Episode 26]

3
00:01:39,070 --> 00:01:40,520
[Lanxin Theater]

4
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:54,509
Laiyi.

5
00:01:57,509 --> 00:01:58,240
Where is she?

6
00:01:58,479 --> 00:01:59,479
What is she doing?

7
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:00,310
Who?

8
00:02:01,230 --> 00:02:02,150
Who do you think?

9
00:02:02,150 --> 00:02:02,870
Miss Ren.

10
00:02:03,350 --> 00:02:04,750
Do you need me to go check?

11
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:05,590
No need.

12
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:08,190
Wait.

13
00:02:11,310 --> 00:02:12,030
What is

14
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:13,000
Le'an doing?

15
00:02:14,030 --> 00:02:15,160
I'd better go check.

16
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:16,310
I didn't ask you to.

17
00:02:16,310 --> 00:02:17,400
I was just asking.

18
00:02:24,550 --> 00:02:25,150
Right,

19
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:26,520
go...

20
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:28,820
see where Qiaoqiao is.

21
00:02:30,310 --> 00:02:31,079
Qiaoqiao?

22
00:02:31,750 --> 00:02:32,400
Go.

23
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:34,430
W-Who's Qiaoqiao?

24
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:54,190
Drink slowly.

25
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:58,280
Uncle.

26
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:02,000
Why are you still up?

27
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:04,940
I'm worried
Qiaoqiao might get hungry at night.

28
00:03:06,190 --> 00:03:07,520
Puppies can't eat this.

29
00:03:07,710 --> 00:03:10,110
It's too salty.
It'll make its fur fall out.

30
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,600
Give it this instead.

31
00:03:15,910 --> 00:03:16,510
Qiaoqiao,

32
00:03:16,750 --> 00:03:17,750
have some treats.

33
00:03:30,590 --> 00:03:32,750
When can Qiaoqiao take a bath?

34
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:35,079
Last time I saw it,

35
00:03:35,190 --> 00:03:37,120
it had mud on its paws.

36
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:39,120
I wanted to bathe it,

37
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:40,590
but Mom said

38
00:03:40,710 --> 00:03:42,400
it couldn't have a bath yet.

39
00:03:42,910 --> 00:03:44,079
Your mom's right.

40
00:03:44,590 --> 00:03:46,870
A puppy shouldn't be bathed
until it's at least 2 months old.

41
00:03:46,870 --> 00:03:48,190
Besides, it's getting chilly.

42
00:03:48,190 --> 00:03:49,560
It'll catch a cold if it takes a bath.

43
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,150
Puppies catch colds too?

44
00:03:51,470 --> 00:03:52,310
Of course.

45
00:03:52,710 --> 00:03:54,030
Puppies can catch colds—

46
00:03:54,030 --> 00:03:55,800
and get sick in plenty of other ways too.

47
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:57,079
Then how can we tell

48
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:59,400
if they're sick?

49
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,120
Their poop changes color.

50
00:04:02,470 --> 00:04:03,870
You can tell if a puppy is sick

51
00:04:03,870 --> 00:04:05,280
by the color of its poop.

52
00:04:05,710 --> 00:04:08,000
But poop smells so bad.

53
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:12,380
I had a puppy when I was little too.

54
00:04:13,030 --> 00:04:13,760
At that time,

55
00:04:14,150 --> 00:04:16,209
I'd crouch beside its kennel to check

56
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:18,560
the color of its poop every morning.

57
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:20,360
At first, I thought it smelled awful too.

58
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:21,310
But after a while,

59
00:04:21,310 --> 00:04:22,390
I got used to it.

60
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:25,120
Uncle.

61
00:04:25,830 --> 00:04:27,000
You're so amazing.

62
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:28,310
What?

63
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:30,400
Tomorrow, I'm going to check

64
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:32,270
Qiaoqiao's poop too.

65
00:04:32,630 --> 00:04:34,560
I just have to hold my breath first.

66
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:38,190
Uncle.

67
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,240
My mom said

68
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:42,310
you've led troops in battle.

69
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:45,510
Are there puppies on the battlefield?

70
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:49,620
There are no puppies on the battlefield.

71
00:04:50,070 --> 00:04:50,950
Would you like

72
00:04:50,950 --> 00:04:53,409
to hear some stories
about the battlefield?

73
00:04:53,720 --> 00:04:54,190
Yes.

74
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:55,650
Alright.

75
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:59,100
Come on, Qiaoqiao, into your kennel.

76
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:02,310
I'll take you

77
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:04,000
for a horsey ride.

78
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:06,360
Let's go.

79
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:08,750
Giddy-up!

80
00:05:10,750 --> 00:05:11,360
Turning!

81
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:13,360
Are you scared? Are you scared?

82
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:14,360
No.

83
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:15,460
Are you scared?

84
00:05:15,630 --> 00:05:17,360
Not scared? Then move a little.

85
00:05:23,870 --> 00:05:24,630
Scared?

86
00:05:51,540 --> 00:05:54,700
[Lanxin Theater]

87
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:54,880
Young Master Qingyi,

88
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:55,830
I found it.

89
00:05:56,600 --> 00:06:00,400
There really is a batch of Red Pills
circulating on the black market.

90
00:06:03,510 --> 00:06:04,800
To save money, customers

91
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:07,600
at the opium dens in Opium Den Alley
bring some of these themselves,

92
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,730
and the owners mostly turn a blind eye.

93
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:15,080
Let's go. To Opium Den Alley.

94
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:55,800
Ren Susu.

95
00:06:58,510 --> 00:06:59,840
What are you doing here?

96
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:01,830
I came to investigate the Red Pills.

97
00:07:01,830 --> 00:07:03,160
Why shouldn't I be here?

98
00:07:04,240 --> 00:07:06,100
You even know about the Red Pills?

99
00:07:06,430 --> 00:07:08,030
Not only do I know about them,

100
00:07:08,070 --> 00:07:08,920
but I also know

101
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:11,890
why you stopped me
from killing Li Rongzhang.

102
00:07:12,310 --> 00:07:14,570
Because he's connected to the Red Pills.

103
00:07:19,390 --> 00:07:20,830
Then let's work together.

104
00:07:20,830 --> 00:07:22,290
We can share information.

105
00:07:24,430 --> 00:07:25,690
As if I'd work with you.

106
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:33,920
I can bring you along,

107
00:07:34,800 --> 00:07:36,930
but you have to agree to one condition.

108
00:07:37,360 --> 00:07:38,290
What condition?

109
00:07:42,510 --> 00:07:43,480
I haven't decided yet.

110
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:44,810
I'll cash it in when I do.

111
00:07:45,070 --> 00:07:46,190
Once I come up with one,

112
00:07:46,190 --> 00:07:47,310
whatever I ask you to do,

113
00:07:47,310 --> 00:07:48,240
you can't say no.

114
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:50,800
I promise.

115
00:07:51,390 --> 00:07:52,520
I don't believe you.

116
00:07:55,950 --> 00:07:56,630
Then...

117
00:08:00,070 --> 00:08:01,270
I swear to heaven.

118
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,390
As long as it doesn't hurt
the people I care about,

119
00:08:04,390 --> 00:08:06,190
I will do whatever you ask.

120
00:08:16,510 --> 00:08:18,160
You'd better not regret it later.

121
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:19,070
I never will.

122
00:08:28,750 --> 00:08:29,810
You little beggar,

123
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,600
you've got a death wish, huh?

124
00:08:31,750 --> 00:08:32,480
Get out here!

125
00:08:32,549 --> 00:08:33,480
Get out, get out!

126
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:35,690
The boss took pity on you

127
00:08:35,750 --> 00:08:37,409
and gave you something to eat.

128
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:38,480
But you,

129
00:08:38,480 --> 00:08:39,610
you pushed your luck

130
00:08:39,669 --> 00:08:41,080
and stole customers' pastries!

131
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:41,750
Get lost!

132
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:47,510
Get lost now!

133
00:08:49,390 --> 00:08:50,120
-Get lost!
-Gentlemen, please.

134
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:50,960
Please come in.

135
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:52,000
-Come in and have another serving.
-Let's go.

136
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:52,720
Come on.

137
00:08:58,790 --> 00:09:00,390
Puppy, eat up.

138
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,480
Eat your fill

139
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:04,340
so you'll have a chance to grow up.

140
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:17,120
Kid, what are you doing here?

141
00:09:17,240 --> 00:09:17,790
Who are you?

142
00:09:17,790 --> 00:09:19,120
W-What do you want?

143
00:09:35,030 --> 00:09:35,600
Here.

144
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:37,670
Go buy yourself something to eat.

145
00:09:37,670 --> 00:09:38,270
No!

146
00:09:38,910 --> 00:09:39,960
I don't need your charity!

147
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:40,890
What's with you?

148
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:43,150
We're giving you money,
and you're refusing it?

149
00:09:43,150 --> 00:09:44,360
Listen up, brat.

150
00:09:45,270 --> 00:09:47,270
If you want to survive in this world,

151
00:09:47,550 --> 00:09:48,360
your pride

152
00:09:48,670 --> 00:09:50,800
is the most useless thing you can have.

153
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:53,510
Take it.

154
00:09:54,390 --> 00:09:55,650
Don't bother with him.

155
00:09:56,150 --> 00:09:57,680
Ungrateful little wretch.

156
00:10:15,150 --> 00:10:15,720
Get up!

157
00:10:16,150 --> 00:10:17,390
Let go of me!

158
00:10:17,390 --> 00:10:18,000
Get up!

159
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,200
-What are you doing?
-You bastard!

160
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,060
Murong Qingyi!

161
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:20,670
Laiyi.

162
00:10:22,180 --> 00:10:22,980
Take him away.

163
00:10:23,630 --> 00:10:24,360
Clean him up,

164
00:10:24,510 --> 00:10:25,670
then send him to the orphanage.

165
00:10:25,670 --> 00:10:26,200
Yes.

166
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:27,270
Let go of me!

167
00:10:27,270 --> 00:10:27,870
Behave.

168
00:10:43,750 --> 00:10:44,550
Such a hassle.

169
00:10:47,550 --> 00:10:48,150
Let's go.

170
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:21,030
This way.

171
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:27,200
What are you thinking about?

172
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:29,910
I was wondering

173
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:32,620
why you seem so familiar with this place.

174
00:11:36,550 --> 00:11:39,120
I came here once before,
when I was delirious.

175
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:06,320
If my brother hadn't found me

176
00:12:06,670 --> 00:12:08,240
and kept holding on to me,

177
00:12:09,440 --> 00:12:10,240
I probably

178
00:12:10,630 --> 00:12:12,030
wouldn't be alive today.

179
00:12:16,030 --> 00:12:17,870
When you were
at the Murong residence before,

180
00:12:17,870 --> 00:12:19,790
didn't you hear them gossip about me,

181
00:12:19,790 --> 00:12:20,910
like I'd been

182
00:12:21,270 --> 00:12:23,600
a troublemaking devil since I was little?

183
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:25,600
So,

184
00:12:26,870 --> 00:12:28,200
what exactly happened?

185
00:12:33,440 --> 00:12:36,270
When I was little, one of our enemies
forced poison down my throat.

186
00:12:36,270 --> 00:12:38,130
They thought I was as good as dead,

187
00:12:39,320 --> 00:12:42,250
so they threw me into the river
to dispose of the body.

188
00:12:43,510 --> 00:12:45,040
Luckily, I was hard to kill.

189
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:47,510
Or maybe I swallowed so much river water

190
00:12:45,750 --> 00:12:49,600
♪ I happened to hear your name ♪

191
00:12:47,790 --> 00:12:49,650
that I threw up most of the poison.

192
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:51,000
Anyway,

193
00:12:50,820 --> 00:12:52,560
♪ And all the memories ♪

194
00:12:51,270 --> 00:12:52,610
someone saved me in the end.

195
00:12:52,610 --> 00:12:55,400
♪ Came flooding back ♪

196
00:12:53,870 --> 00:12:54,790
Who did it?

197
00:12:56,390 --> 00:12:58,240
♪ There I stood in the falling snow ♪

198
00:12:58,240 --> 00:12:59,080
I can't remember.

199
00:12:58,260 --> 00:13:00,700
♪ Wrapped in my coat ♪

200
00:12:59,870 --> 00:13:01,750
I only recall a few blurry images.

201
00:13:01,470 --> 00:13:03,590
♪ My heart pounding ♪

202
00:13:05,550 --> 00:13:06,360
Open your mouth!

203
00:13:05,720 --> 00:13:07,600
♪ Walking down that old road ♪

204
00:13:07,650 --> 00:13:09,560
♪ Stopping every few steps ♪

205
00:13:10,900 --> 00:13:12,710
♪ In the misty train car ♪

206
00:13:12,740 --> 00:13:15,930
♪ I wish I could ask you once more ♪

207
00:13:16,030 --> 00:13:16,840
Maybe

208
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:18,200
the poison damaged my brain.

209
00:13:17,280 --> 00:13:21,180
♪ If you have any ♪

210
00:13:21,260 --> 00:13:23,380
♪ New corny jokes to tell ♪

211
00:13:22,910 --> 00:13:24,270
You were delirious.

212
00:13:25,540 --> 00:13:27,050
♪ I'm running ♪

213
00:13:25,750 --> 00:13:26,630
So...

214
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:27,790
So what?

215
00:13:27,700 --> 00:13:29,880
♪ Running toward you ♪

216
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:30,200
I bet you're not about to
say anything nice.

217
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:32,330
♪ From the day I thought ♪

218
00:13:31,390 --> 00:13:33,870
Want to mock me as a walking jinx

219
00:13:32,400 --> 00:13:35,500
♪ I succeeded in forgetting you ♪

220
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:36,030
or scold me for having a damaged brain

221
00:13:36,030 --> 00:13:37,670
and bringing misfortune
to everyone around me?

222
00:13:36,810 --> 00:13:38,700
♪ Facing the past ♪

223
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:39,200
What else do you want to say?

224
00:13:38,720 --> 00:13:41,060
♪ With you inside ♪

225
00:13:41,250 --> 00:13:43,020
♪ My resolve crumbles ♪

226
00:13:43,050 --> 00:13:45,260
♪ Immediately ♪

227
00:13:45,290 --> 00:13:47,750
♪ I'm running ♪

228
00:13:47,390 --> 00:13:48,390
I want to stroke its fur.

229
00:13:47,870 --> 00:13:49,730
♪ Running toward you ♪

230
00:13:50,520 --> 00:13:52,900
♪ No matter how much gossip there is ♪

231
00:13:52,930 --> 00:13:54,940
♪ I have the courage ♪

232
00:13:55,050 --> 00:14:00,580
♪ I know you're not far away ♪

233
00:14:01,090 --> 00:14:04,700
[Penglai Opium Den]

234
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:04,120
♪ Having loved you deeply ♪

235
00:14:03,600 --> 00:14:04,840
We've never sold

236
00:14:04,150 --> 00:14:07,450
♪ Was the best decision I've made ♪

237
00:14:05,150 --> 00:14:07,600
that stuff you mentioned in our opium den.

238
00:14:07,870 --> 00:14:08,480
But

239
00:14:08,790 --> 00:14:09,750
I've heard of it.

240
00:14:10,200 --> 00:14:10,870
It's said

241
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,510
that only poor people smoke it

242
00:14:12,510 --> 00:14:13,640
because it's cheap.

243
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:14,320
However,

244
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:16,030
the side effects are pretty severe.

245
00:14:16,030 --> 00:14:17,560
And supply is often cut off.

246
00:14:18,840 --> 00:14:19,320
By the way,

247
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:20,150
I also heard

248
00:14:20,390 --> 00:14:22,960
that there's a new, refined batch

249
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:24,240
coming to Nancheng soon.

250
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:25,120
Lots of people

251
00:14:25,480 --> 00:14:27,240
are waiting with bated breath for it.

252
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:29,360
Do you know who handles it,

253
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:30,840
what the route is,

254
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:32,240
or where they're headed?

255
00:14:32,670 --> 00:14:34,360
You're really putting me on the spot here.

256
00:14:34,360 --> 00:14:35,150
Think about it—

257
00:14:35,150 --> 00:14:37,000
that's their money-making business.

258
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,330
Why would they go around

259
00:14:38,390 --> 00:14:40,590
broadcasting it to their competitors?

260
00:14:44,630 --> 00:14:46,670
We have to find
that shipment of Red Pills.

261
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:48,250
[Penglai Opium Den]

262
00:14:48,510 --> 00:14:50,360
Didn't you say we'd share information?

263
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:51,020
Go on, then.

264
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:58,240
You head back first.

265
00:14:58,240 --> 00:14:59,670
I've got something else to take care of.

266
00:14:59,670 --> 00:15:00,510
We'll talk when I get back.

267
00:15:00,510 --> 00:15:03,750
[Penglai Opium Den]

268
00:15:05,960 --> 00:15:07,360
Why are you following me?

269
00:15:09,150 --> 00:15:10,840
Since we agreed to investigate together,

270
00:15:10,840 --> 00:15:13,510
please, Young Master Qingyi,
have some basic trust in me.

271
00:15:13,510 --> 00:15:15,030
After all, I never pried into

272
00:15:15,030 --> 00:15:16,000
your sources of information,

273
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:16,550
did I?

274
00:15:17,840 --> 00:15:19,640
Who said I'm going to follow you?

275
00:15:20,240 --> 00:15:21,500
I just wanted to ask...

276
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:25,130
What should we do about this puppy?

277
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:28,840
Return it to its owner, of course.

278
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:30,270
So the esteemed principal
of the aviation school

279
00:15:30,270 --> 00:15:32,200
is stealing a little kid's dog now?

280
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:35,820
Who says it's someone else's dog?

281
00:15:36,030 --> 00:15:37,890
So what if I want to keep it myself?

282
00:15:52,270 --> 00:15:54,730
Clean it up
and send it to that little beggar.

283
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,200
Tao, how'd it go?

284
00:16:02,980 --> 00:16:06,810
[Tao, Young Man]

285
00:16:03,790 --> 00:16:05,390
We searched all over Nancheng

286
00:16:05,390 --> 00:16:07,720
but couldn't find this pattern anywhere.

287
00:16:08,110 --> 00:16:09,310
However, I did notice

288
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:10,030
a few unusual trains

289
00:16:10,030 --> 00:16:11,600
at the station recently.

290
00:16:11,750 --> 00:16:13,480
The trains that normally come through

291
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:15,790
have straight, tube-shaped smokestacks.

292
00:16:15,790 --> 00:16:18,030
But those trains' smokestacks
are shaped like this,

293
00:16:18,030 --> 00:16:18,890
like trumpets.

294
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:21,960
I've never seen anything like them.

295
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:22,600
And

296
00:16:22,750 --> 00:16:23,390
those trains

297
00:16:23,390 --> 00:16:25,270
only arrive and depart
in the middle of the night.

298
00:16:25,270 --> 00:16:27,470
Even the cargo is unloaded before dawn.

299
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:29,740
Those people act very suspiciously too.

300
00:16:30,150 --> 00:16:31,200
Could you tell

301
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:32,870
what they were unloading?

302
00:16:32,870 --> 00:16:33,630
No.

303
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:36,120
The train station is surrounded by troops.

304
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:37,650
I didn't dare get too close.

305
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:38,790
But

306
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:40,030
during the day, those trains

307
00:16:40,030 --> 00:16:41,510
are parked on the open tracks

308
00:16:41,510 --> 00:16:42,510
beside the station.

309
00:16:42,510 --> 00:16:43,640
I can take you there.

310
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:44,510
Let's go.

311
00:16:47,350 --> 00:16:51,430
[Lanxin Theater]

312
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:08,000
Come in.

313
00:17:10,550 --> 00:17:11,240
Uncle.

314
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:13,400
Do you want some?

315
00:17:14,480 --> 00:17:15,810
What have you got there?

316
00:17:18,510 --> 00:17:20,790
Broad beans I stole from the storeroom.

317
00:17:22,160 --> 00:17:23,200
I can't eat those.

318
00:17:23,349 --> 00:17:23,880
Sit.

319
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:29,590
Uncle,

320
00:17:29,830 --> 00:17:31,480
what book are you reading?

321
00:17:32,790 --> 00:17:34,590
A boring military book.

322
00:17:35,830 --> 00:17:37,640
Then why are you reading it?

323
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:39,970
My storybooks are much more interesting.

324
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:41,640
In this world,

325
00:17:42,070 --> 00:17:44,530
you don't always
get to do only what you like.

326
00:17:47,830 --> 00:17:48,590
Qingyi,

327
00:17:49,270 --> 00:17:50,160
this world

328
00:17:50,640 --> 00:17:52,900
won't change just because you want it to.

329
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:04,510
Uncle, what are you thinking about?

330
00:18:06,270 --> 00:18:08,070
Thinking about a family member.

331
00:18:09,590 --> 00:18:11,030
If you miss him,

332
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:12,790
I won't go home tonight.

333
00:18:13,070 --> 00:18:15,270
I'll stay and keep you company tonight.

334
00:18:15,440 --> 00:18:16,200
Why?

335
00:18:17,350 --> 00:18:19,030
Whenever I feel lonely,

336
00:18:19,200 --> 00:18:21,330
Mom always stays with me while I sleep.

337
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:26,610
What about your dad?

338
00:18:26,960 --> 00:18:28,160
Doesn't he stay with you?

339
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:29,640
Which dad do you mean?

340
00:18:31,750 --> 00:18:32,720
"Which dad?"

341
00:18:33,480 --> 00:18:34,680
You have lots of dads?

342
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:37,440
Of course.

343
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:38,960
Sometimes,

344
00:18:39,480 --> 00:18:42,720
I wish Uncle Wu, who sells little cakes,

345
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:43,750
were my dad.

346
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:45,240
Sometimes,

347
00:18:45,240 --> 00:18:46,550
I wish

348
00:18:46,550 --> 00:18:49,080
Aniu, who makes sugar figurines,
were my dad.

349
00:18:49,110 --> 00:18:51,200
And... you're good-looking.

350
00:18:51,830 --> 00:18:53,830
I wouldn't mind having you as my dad.

351
00:18:57,790 --> 00:18:58,850
You little rascal.

352
00:18:59,070 --> 00:19:01,670
So anyone who gives you treats
is your dad, huh?

353
00:19:09,310 --> 00:19:09,880
Le'an!

354
00:19:10,640 --> 00:19:11,440
Uncle,

355
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:13,110
I can't breathe.

356
00:19:13,830 --> 00:19:15,490
This is an allergic reaction.

357
00:19:15,830 --> 00:19:16,400
Someone!

358
00:19:16,510 --> 00:19:18,770
Get the car! We're going to the hospital!

359
00:19:23,070 --> 00:19:24,330
How could this happen?

360
00:19:25,310 --> 00:19:26,640
What did you feed Le'an?

361
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:28,000
I told you long ago

362
00:19:28,240 --> 00:19:29,570
to stay away from my son.

363
00:19:32,590 --> 00:19:33,400
You never told me,

364
00:19:33,400 --> 00:19:34,930
so how was I supposed to know

365
00:19:35,880 --> 00:19:36,750
that my son...

366
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:41,200
is allergic to broad beans just like me?

367
00:19:54,070 --> 00:19:56,750
The child has a severe allergic reaction
to broad beans.

368
00:19:56,750 --> 00:19:59,010
You've been far too careless as parents.

369
00:19:59,030 --> 00:20:00,090
In cases like this,

370
00:20:00,270 --> 00:20:01,680
the child's immediate family members

371
00:20:01,680 --> 00:20:03,480
must also have the same allergy.

372
00:20:03,880 --> 00:20:05,740
You should've been aware of that.

373
00:20:05,830 --> 00:20:09,360
How could you let the child
come into contact with the allergen?

374
00:20:23,590 --> 00:20:25,590
How much longer
are you going to lie to me?

375
00:20:25,590 --> 00:20:29,520
Do you just enjoy jerking me around
and keeping me in the dark like this?

376
00:20:30,110 --> 00:20:31,030
His age,

377
00:20:31,310 --> 00:20:32,270
his looks,

378
00:20:32,270 --> 00:20:34,110
even his allergy—everything matches.

379
00:20:34,110 --> 00:20:34,960
Ren Susu,

380
00:20:36,110 --> 00:20:37,770
are you still going to deny it?

381
00:20:55,790 --> 00:20:57,160
Le'an even told me today

382
00:20:57,960 --> 00:21:00,270
how nice it would be if I were his father.

383
00:21:01,920 --> 00:21:03,320
What exactly do you want?

384
00:21:04,270 --> 00:21:05,440
I'm his father.

385
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:08,260
I have the right to know he exists.

386
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:12,480
Besides,

387
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:15,030
he's a human being.

388
00:21:15,270 --> 00:21:16,550
And he's just a child.

389
00:21:17,350 --> 00:21:19,270
He's not a tool for you to get back at me.

390
00:21:19,270 --> 00:21:22,110
You really think I'd use my own child
to get revenge on you?

391
00:21:22,110 --> 00:21:24,170
I've raised him by myself for 6 years.

392
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:26,270
Who was it that said you hated me

393
00:21:26,270 --> 00:21:28,160
and never wanted to see me again
for the rest of your life?

394
00:21:28,160 --> 00:21:29,290
How could I let Le'an

395
00:21:29,350 --> 00:21:31,680
have a father
who hates him and his mother?

396
00:21:37,350 --> 00:21:38,790
Look at your family.

397
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:40,700
Then look at yourself.

398
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:42,680
Do you honestly think
you'd make a good father?

399
00:21:42,680 --> 00:21:43,880
I never asked you to!

400
00:21:54,920 --> 00:21:55,640
Forget it.

401
00:22:00,550 --> 00:22:01,720
I told you not to follow me!

402
00:22:01,720 --> 00:22:02,780
Didn't you hear me?

403
00:22:05,960 --> 00:22:06,640
I saved you,

404
00:22:06,640 --> 00:22:08,900
so I have to take responsibility for you.

405
00:22:09,440 --> 00:22:10,300
I don't want it.

406
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:12,490
I never asked you to save me.

407
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:23,590
Papa, Mama,
come out quickly and put out the fire!

408
00:22:23,590 --> 00:22:24,510
Susu!

409
00:22:24,590 --> 00:22:26,310
-Susu!
-Come out and put out the fire!

410
00:22:26,310 --> 00:22:27,530
-Come out!
-Susu!

411
00:22:28,060 --> 00:22:30,120
-Susu!
-Come out and put out the fire!

412
00:22:47,070 --> 00:22:48,800
You can't take it upon yourself

413
00:22:48,880 --> 00:22:50,880
to deny me the right to be his father.

414
00:22:51,030 --> 00:22:53,230
I simply don't want you to be his father.

415
00:22:54,200 --> 00:22:56,200
You're just an ungrateful bastard.

416
00:22:59,640 --> 00:23:01,370
Do you think you're any better?

417
00:23:03,590 --> 00:23:04,640
You're so calculating

418
00:23:04,640 --> 00:23:05,750
and cold-blooded.

419
00:23:05,750 --> 00:23:07,750
What gives you the right to judge me?

420
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:09,680
We're the same.

421
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:12,160
We only bring misfortune
to those around us.

422
00:23:12,160 --> 00:23:13,020
Satisfied now?

423
00:23:16,640 --> 00:23:17,640
So please,

424
00:23:18,790 --> 00:23:20,590
stay away from Le'an from now on.

425
00:23:55,310 --> 00:23:56,640
Mom.

426
00:24:04,920 --> 00:24:05,640
Le'an.

427
00:24:07,920 --> 00:24:10,120
Are you still feeling unwell anywhere?

428
00:24:10,590 --> 00:24:11,590
Mom,

429
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:13,790
don't cry.

430
00:24:17,240 --> 00:24:18,070
Mom won't cry.

431
00:24:20,240 --> 00:24:22,100
Mom will go get you some hot water.

432
00:25:04,960 --> 00:25:06,070
Gu.

433
00:25:06,830 --> 00:25:07,630
Madam Murong,

434
00:25:09,270 --> 00:25:11,030
you really shouldn't drink anymore.

435
00:25:11,030 --> 00:25:13,200
Young Miss Jinrui
has warned me several times

436
00:25:13,200 --> 00:25:14,730
not to sell you any alcohol.

437
00:25:27,400 --> 00:25:28,750
Can I drink?

438
00:25:30,830 --> 00:25:32,640
Can I?

439
00:25:32,640 --> 00:25:33,070
Yes.

440
00:25:33,550 --> 00:25:34,000
Yes.

441
00:25:34,160 --> 00:25:35,270
Yes, you can.

442
00:26:07,110 --> 00:26:07,680
Sir,

443
00:26:07,880 --> 00:26:08,940
here is your drink.

444
00:27:23,680 --> 00:27:25,280
Don't recognize me anymore?

445
00:27:53,590 --> 00:27:54,960
You're back.

446
00:27:57,270 --> 00:27:58,750
It really is you.

447
00:28:03,480 --> 00:28:05,540
Back then, whenever anything happened

448
00:28:05,540 --> 00:28:08,030
among Nancheng's
political or business elite,

449
00:28:08,030 --> 00:28:09,760
you always knew, Madam Murong.

450
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:10,550
What?

451
00:28:11,390 --> 00:28:13,750
I came back, and you didn't hear a thing?

452
00:28:27,640 --> 00:28:30,570
You came back just to
gloat over our family's misery.

453
00:28:34,790 --> 00:28:35,510
Family?

454
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:39,930
Have you forgotten, Madam Murong?

455
00:28:40,640 --> 00:28:42,840
We stopped being family a long time ago.

456
00:28:59,350 --> 00:29:00,750
How could I forget?

457
00:29:01,680 --> 00:29:04,070
You would rather endure 3 stab wounds

458
00:29:06,200 --> 00:29:09,160
than remain a member of the Murong family.

459
00:29:10,880 --> 00:29:13,160
How could I ever forget that?

460
00:29:20,640 --> 00:29:22,070
Look at your family.

461
00:29:22,750 --> 00:29:24,010
Then look at yourself.

462
00:29:24,790 --> 00:29:27,390
Do you honestly think
you'd make a good father?

463
00:29:48,240 --> 00:29:49,900
When you had your first child,

464
00:29:50,440 --> 00:29:51,770
what were you thinking?

465
00:29:58,960 --> 00:30:00,750
Why are you asking that?

466
00:30:03,350 --> 00:30:04,200
Just curious.

467
00:30:15,510 --> 00:30:17,310
When I had Jinrui...

468
00:30:20,790 --> 00:30:23,720
your father and I
were marching and fighting in a war.

469
00:30:25,720 --> 00:30:26,640
We had no choice

470
00:30:26,640 --> 00:30:29,960
but to leave her
with a local family in Wuchi.

471
00:30:32,400 --> 00:30:34,270
It wasn't until 7 or 8 years later

472
00:30:36,030 --> 00:30:37,440
that we brought her home.

473
00:30:44,110 --> 00:30:46,440
By then, she'd grown into an ignorant,

474
00:30:48,640 --> 00:30:50,720
rough, and unsophisticated child.

475
00:30:54,480 --> 00:30:56,790
I felt I owed her so much.

476
00:30:58,310 --> 00:30:59,960
If she'd grown up by my side,

477
00:30:59,960 --> 00:31:02,090
she wouldn't have turned out this way.

478
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:06,510
So I swore...

479
00:31:08,070 --> 00:31:09,720
I'd make it up to her.

480
00:31:13,720 --> 00:31:14,640
Yes.

481
00:31:16,960 --> 00:31:18,350
You failed Qingyu,

482
00:31:18,790 --> 00:31:19,830
failed Jinrui,

483
00:31:20,720 --> 00:31:22,240
and failed Li Boze.

484
00:31:22,720 --> 00:31:23,680
Only me—

485
00:31:24,550 --> 00:31:27,010
even though back then you hit me,
scolded me,

486
00:31:27,240 --> 00:31:29,100
wronged me, and looked down on me—

487
00:31:29,160 --> 00:31:30,420
it was always my fault,

488
00:31:31,200 --> 00:31:31,830
right?

489
00:31:54,160 --> 00:31:55,160
Why?

490
00:32:01,960 --> 00:32:05,560
Why were our two families' babies
switched by mistake back then?

491
00:32:08,680 --> 00:32:11,400
Why did a wretch like you
turn out to be my son?

492
00:32:12,590 --> 00:32:14,270
Why is it that you're my son,

493
00:32:14,270 --> 00:32:16,110
yet at the most critical moment,

494
00:32:16,110 --> 00:32:17,310
-your dad was about to be assassinated...
-Enough! I don't want to hear it!

495
00:32:17,310 --> 00:32:18,510
Enough with the whys!

496
00:32:38,110 --> 00:32:39,970
I'm getting married in a few days.

497
00:32:42,310 --> 00:32:43,770
Madam Murong, please come

498
00:32:44,640 --> 00:32:46,370
have a few drinks at my wedding.

499
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:48,960
What?

500
00:32:50,480 --> 00:32:52,010
You deserve to get married?

501
00:32:53,590 --> 00:32:55,920
What makes you think you deserve to marry?

502
00:32:59,920 --> 00:33:03,120
Whether I marry or not—
do you have any right to judge that?

503
00:33:05,550 --> 00:33:06,310
All these years,

504
00:33:06,310 --> 00:33:09,480
I've fought my way through
a hail of bullets, step by step.

505
00:33:09,480 --> 00:33:12,160
Instead of asking whether I'm tired,
in pain, or hurt,

506
00:33:12,160 --> 00:33:15,020
you open your mouth and say
I don't deserve to marry.

507
00:33:17,030 --> 00:33:18,640
Before today, I often wondered

508
00:33:18,640 --> 00:33:19,970
whether someone like me

509
00:33:20,400 --> 00:33:22,030
was qualified to be a father

510
00:33:22,680 --> 00:33:24,410
or deserved a complete family.

511
00:33:25,720 --> 00:33:26,960
But after seeing you today,

512
00:33:26,960 --> 00:33:28,220
I finally understand.

513
00:33:28,550 --> 00:33:30,160
If even you can be a mother,

514
00:33:30,550 --> 00:33:31,810
why can't I be a father?

515
00:33:32,200 --> 00:33:33,200
At the very least,

516
00:33:34,550 --> 00:33:36,000
I won't let my child

517
00:33:37,960 --> 00:33:39,890
relive the tragedy I went through.

518
00:34:10,150 --> 00:34:11,110
My child!

519
00:34:32,820 --> 00:34:34,889
[Zarry Grand Hotel]

520
00:34:35,100 --> 00:34:37,429
[Two days later]

521
00:34:55,590 --> 00:34:56,280
Miss Ren,

522
00:34:56,630 --> 00:34:57,360
you're here.

523
00:34:59,400 --> 00:35:00,760
Where did he take Le'an?

524
00:35:02,550 --> 00:35:04,350
You'll know when the time comes.

525
00:35:10,760 --> 00:35:11,630
By the way, Mother,

526
00:35:11,630 --> 00:35:14,230
why do we even need to
come to Qingyi's wedding?

527
00:35:14,440 --> 00:35:17,070
Have you forgotten that back then he...

528
00:35:27,400 --> 00:35:28,070
Mother,

529
00:35:28,590 --> 00:35:30,000
why is Fang Mulan here?

530
00:35:30,480 --> 00:35:32,360
Qingyi invited her too?

531
00:35:33,710 --> 00:35:34,360
The bride and groom are here.

532
00:35:34,360 --> 00:35:35,960
The bride and groom are here.

533
00:35:38,960 --> 00:35:41,030
♪ How much love ♪

534
00:35:41,050 --> 00:35:43,150
♪ Is enough to be wasted? ♪

535
00:35:45,760 --> 00:35:47,530
♪ I haven't forgiven you ♪

536
00:35:47,550 --> 00:35:49,640
♪ So don't you forgive me ♪

537
00:35:51,960 --> 00:35:54,340
♪ Let the wildfire ♪

538
00:35:54,420 --> 00:35:57,510
♪ Consume us and burn us to ashes ♪

539
00:35:58,210 --> 00:36:00,870
♪ Still, we choose to be moths ♪

540
00:36:00,950 --> 00:36:03,390
♪ Flying into the flames ♪

541
00:36:05,570 --> 00:36:07,180
♪ Must it take heartache ♪

542
00:36:07,240 --> 00:36:09,330
♪ To know my heart belongs to you? ♪

543
00:36:09,780 --> 00:36:12,100
♪ Hearts cold no more ♪

544
00:36:12,120 --> 00:36:13,720
♪ Is every sweet dream ♪

545
00:36:13,810 --> 00:36:15,830
♪ Destined to fade away? ♪

546
00:36:16,380 --> 00:36:18,770
♪ Don't let it end in smoke ♪
